# Who gets asked to review what.
#
# Every line here names the same person, because there is one maintainer. Said
# plainly so the file is not mistaken for more than it is:
#
#   - it auto-requests a review on every pull request, so nothing arrives
#     unassigned and nothing sits waiting for someone to notice it;
#   - it puts an owner beside a path in the review UI; and
#   - it blocks nothing. CODEOWNERS is only enforced where a branch requires
#     review from code owners, and `main` has no protection rule. Turning one
#     on is the step that gives this file teeth — until then it is routing,
#     not a gate.
#
# The path entries below are redundant today and deliberate anyway. They mark
# the files where an unreviewed change is expensive rather than merely wrong,
# and they become load-bearing the moment a second person has push access —
# which is exactly when nobody will remember to write them.

# Everything, unless something below is more specific. Last match wins.
*                           @Pr1nted

# The live service: accounts, tokens and the relay. It holds account records
# and issues what everything downstream trusts, so a change here reaches every
# player at once and cannot be rolled back by not installing an update.
/net/                       @Pr1nted

# Terms. Changing any of these changes what a contribution or a download
# means, which is not a code review. The two under net/ come after the
# directory above them on purpose: last match wins, so the specific rule has
# to be the later one.
/LICENSE                    @Pr1nted
/CLA.md                     @Pr1nted
/CLA-SIGNATURES.md          @Pr1nted
/SECURITY.md                @Pr1nted
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md         @Pr1nted
/CONTRIBUTING.md            @Pr1nted
/net/TERMS.md               @Pr1nted
/net/PRIVACY.md             @Pr1nted

# The security boundaries themselves — the mod sandbox and the multiplayer
# stack. SECURITY.md explains why these two directories are where a bug costs
# the most.
/src/mods/                  @Pr1nted
/src/net/                   @Pr1nted

# Attribution. NOTICE.md, data/credits.txt and the credits screen are all
# generated from this one file, and the test suite fails if they drift.
/tools/provenance.json      @Pr1nted
/data/licenses/             @Pr1nted

# Release and signing plumbing. What ships, and from where.
/.github/workflows/         @Pr1nted
/tools/release.py           @Pr1nted
/packaging/                 @Pr1nted
